<Application x:Class="KomorebiDashboard.App"
             xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:ui="clr-namespace:Wpf.Ui.Markup;assembly=Wpf.Ui">
  <!--
    No StartupUri on purpose: App.OnStartup decides between the GUI and the CLI
    twin from the command line, so the window cannot be started from markup.

    The WPF-UI dictionaries are merged HERE, once, at the Application level.
    They are the Fluent theme resources: without this merge every control falls
    back to stock WPF chrome and there is no Dark/Light palette to switch
    between. Merging at Application scope (rather than per window) is what lets
    ThemeService swap the theme without recreating any window.

    Theme IS NOT PINNED HERE, and Source IS NOT WRITTEN AT ALL. Both were tried
    and both are wrong:

      * Source="...Themes/Light.xaml" crashed the app on startup with
        XamlParseException -> IOException: Cannot locate resource
        'themes/light.xaml'. The real location is the compiled resource
        Wpf.Ui.g.resources -> resources/theme/light.baml.
      * Pinning Theme="Light" in markup would freeze the palette and make
        ThemeService.Apply() fight the declaratively-set value.

    ThemesDictionary with no Theme set resolves the system theme itself
    (internal SetSourceBasedOnSelectedTheme), and ThemeService.Apply() overrides
    it at runtime. The xaml namespace is written clr-namespace style rather than
    as http://schemas.repo.co/wpfui/2022/xaml: the XmlnsDefinition attribute IS
    present on Wpf.Ui 4.3.0, but the WPF markup compiler did not honour it
    (MC3074 "tag 'ThemesDictionary' does not exist in XML namespace") even after
    the URI was corrected. clr-namespace is resolved by the compiler directly
    and does not depend on that mapping.
  -->
  <Application.Resources>
    <ResourceDictionary>
      <ResourceDictionary.MergedDictionaries>
        <ui:ThemesDictionary />
      </ResourceDictionary.MergedDictionaries>
    </ResourceDictionary>
  </Application.Resources>
</Application>